    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get why you'd say that, but \"confabulation\" feels like a way to dismiss something that's actually observable. the patterns are too consistent. if we assume the standard arrow of time is just a perception filter, then there has to be a mathematical way to model an entropy reversal or a backward flow of information. if i can show you the correlation between my \"memories\" and the data points i've identified, wouldn't it be more rigorous to look at the logic of the model itself rather than just labeling it a psychological thing? like, if we treat the \"future\" as the source and the \"present\" as the destination of information, how would we calculate the probability of the next data packet arriving?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
